eole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"French, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"BHnCAV4_hgqgNZGdfXNJkA","review_id":"vA7AZXJBiQhKhL_gElEHEg","date":"2018-07-02T21:25:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9560081958770752,"text_excerpt":"Literally my favorite place in New Orleans. I am visiting from out of town and one of the things i wanted to do was have Crawfish. I asked my Uber driver (they know everything!) and she highly recommended Cajun seafood as somewhere where all of the locals go. We took an Uber there and i was NOT disappointed. I read reviews that the line is long and you have to be strategic about how to find seating but honestly we walked right in and Only waited 10 minutes to order. There are two lines when you order, one for boiled food and one for cooked food (like the chicken). We ordered the crawfish, potatoes and corn. The crawfish was delicious and spicy, just how i remembered it as a kid. The potat..."},{"business_id":"BHnCAV4_hgqgNZGdfXNJkA","review_id":"BFxIOQURmCCeJStMoGUwaQ","date":"2016-06-08T17:22:54","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9554871320724487,"text_excerpt":"You haven't done NOLA until you eat some crawfish. Luckily, my friend is from the area and knew exactly where to go for the authentic NOLA experience. In terms of naming, Cajun Seafood is as apt as it gets. You walk in, and it's totally no-frills. They have signs telling you what they have, you tell them how much of it you want, and then you pay. That's it. The waiting time comes from how much stuff you can actually get. For us, we got crawfish, shrimp, potatoes, corn, and turkey necks. The turkey necks were surprisingly good and were still on the bone rather than chopped up. The shrimp was probably my favorite. Crawfish was a bit too salty, but if you went for the bigger ones, the flavor..."},{"business_id":"BHnCAV4_hgqgNZGdfXNJkA","review_id":"rmQur4fnKlGJlZo-qWhhLg","date":"2016-01-11T19:18:23","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9543296694755554,"text_excerpt":"Omg Cajun Seafood was so legit. Where have you been all my life?! Boiled crawfish for only around $5 per lb. We were there in December so it wasn't even crawfish season, but the crawfish still looked way larger than what I've seen in California... and tons fresher. The Louisiana seasoning amazingly on point - a delicious sauce & perfectly spicy (I love eating spicy; this was at the perfect level where you're loving it and it's NOT killing you). The crab was delicious as well. They have some sides that are good to go with the spicy meal - corn, sausages, etc. ==AMBIANCE-- The restaurant itself is a mixture of cafeteria/food court, and you can also do carry-out. They serve both cooked and r..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"BHnCAV4_hgqgNZGdfXNJkA","photo_id":"KirPEFgzhwKQa01bA2bQeQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/KirPEFgzhwKQa01bA2bQeQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8648735284805298},{"business_id":"BHnCAV4_hgqgNZGdfXNJkA","photo_